{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>He declares His words</b> — the sense is: He declared His words, which are the commandments, to Jacob. And likewise the meaning of <b>His statutes and His ordinances</b>, for they are the cause of the rain's falling in its season, as written in the section of והיה אם שמוע (Deuteronomy 11:13 ff.): \"If you heed My commandments... I will give the rain of your land in its season.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 147, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:03.477786722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}